  "worked_solution": "First, we write the equation in standard form by bringing all of the terms to the left-hand side. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+22(x+1) & =-100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+22x+22+100 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+22x+122 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the roots of a quadratic equation using the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the coefficients are $a=1,\\,b=22,$ and $c=122.$ Substituting these values into the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-22\\pm \\sqrt{(22)^{2}-4(1)(122)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-22\\pm \\sqrt{484-488}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-22\\pm \\sqrt{-4}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-22\\pm 2\\,\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-11\\pm 1\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-11+\\text{i}$ and $x=-11-\\text{i}.$",
